// CotSC: English translation extracted from bg1100_baldurs_gate.d
// Original English strings preserved exactly. Translate text inside ~...~ only.

@1 = ~Pardon me for asking but I was wondering if you could direct me to Flaming Fist quarters.~
@2 = ~Sure. It's just south-west from here. You won't miss it.~
@3 = ~We are new in the city. We don't know yet.~
@4 = ~I'll tell you, once you pull your hand out of my pocket, thief.~
@5 = ~Out of my sight! You're wasting my time.~
@6 = ~Thank you so much. For everything.~
@7 = ~Oh, I see. I guess I'll ask someone else.~
@8 = ~Eh... fine. Have it your way. I wanted to avoid bloodshed.~
@9 = ~You're no fun. Fine! Leave as I cannot deal with you anymore!~
@10 = ~He he… fountain.~
@11 = ~May your time in our city be a memorable experience, traveller.~
@12 = ~If you're interested in legends of Baldur's Gate and our rich history you should seek Theo the Historian. Last I heard he was sharing his knowledge at Purple Wyrm Inn. You should visit that place.~
@13 = ~Be careful, friend. Iron Throne seems dangerous. Very dangerous.~
@14 = ~That Phandalyn is really driving me insane. He looked me up and down, put his hand on my shoulder and said that I am pure. Then he did the same on my friend Lucy. She is a bit... eccentric, to put it mildly. But she isn't a bad-bad person, more like a... misdirected person. Phandalyn wasted no time and simply got his weapon out and attacked without warning. Lucy ran, I tried to talk some sense into him but this arbitrary paladin wannabe shoved me to the side, and lent no ear to my pleas. Lucy is now terrified to walk the streets alone, in fear she'll meet him. Watch yourselves if you see him.~
@15 = ~Come to Baldur's Gate, they said. You'll have some peace and quiet, they said. Have fun trying to walk five steps without children wanting to ride you like a horse, or pet and cuddle you because they find you cute. Meeh.~
@16 = ~Nasty times befell us. Prices go up, Amn plans a bloodthirsty war, and I am tired of all this. Mark my words, one day this whole world will burn.~
@17 = ~World will burn anyway when mighty Tiax accomplishes his destiny. You will be a slave, or you shall perish.~
@18 = ~Can anyone shut this blasted gnome up, or should I do the honour?~
@19 = ~Riiight.~
@20 = ~Aren't you those responsible for clearing Nashkel mines? You are THE heroes. I am honoured to be in our presence.~
@21 = ~As much as I enjoy meeting new friends, I kindly ask you to keep your distance. All the weapons don't inspire much trust.~
@22 = ~There is a nasty paladin called Phandalyn in these parts. He attacked me without giving me a chance to reason with him. He uses his innate powers or something and thinks he can declare you good or bad. It's incredibly judgmental to do so. I have lived here my whole life and I never experienced such prejudice in this city. If you meet him, just walk out right away.~
@23 = ~A goblin warned us about a paladin called Phandalyn. He claims that Phandalyn attacked him without giving him a chance to reason, and that the paladin judges people as good or bad using some kind of innate power. The goblin urged us to leave immediately if we meet him.~
